# Line endings.
#
# `* text=auto` alone normalises text to LF *in the repository* but checks it
# out with the platform's native ending — CRLF on Windows. Prettier is
# configured with `endOfLine: "lf"`, so on a Windows checkout it reports every
# such file as misformatted and `pnpm check` fails, while the same commit passes
# in Linux CI. The blobs were always LF; only the working tree differed. An
# explicit `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the blob on every platform.
#
# `* text=auto` is kept as the default because it is binary-safe: Git detects
# binary content and leaves it alone. The per-format rules below only ever apply
# to files Git has already classified as text, so adding a PNG or a font later
# cannot be corrupted by them. There is deliberately no blanket `* text eol=lf`,
# which would force every file — including binaries — through the text filter.

* text=auto

# TypeScript and JavaScript, in every module flavour the toolchain accepts.
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.mts   text eol=lf
*.cts   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf

# Data, configuration and documentation.
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Shell scripts (scripts/backup). Bash reads a carriage return as part of the
# command, so a CRLF checkout does not run at all.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Database schema and reviewed migration SQL.
*.prisma text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf

# Environment templates: .env.example and apps/web/.env.local.example.
# Real environment files are never committed.
*.example text eol=lf

# Owner-approved brand artwork is copied byte-for-byte from its immutable pack.
apps/web/public/brand/*.svg -text

# Extensionless dotfiles, which no wildcard above reaches.
.editorconfig   text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.npmrc          text eol=lf
.nvmrc          text eol=lf
.prettierignore text eol=lf
